{
 "about": "D-SINK-40, D-SINK-41, D-SINK-42 (2026-10-29): where provider data may send this machine. One file, two implementations (CLAUDE.md: a rule in two languages gets one shared fixture). `hosts`: every spelling of a URL host, its class (bin/helper 01-core.py host_class / Model.hostClass; one of `classes`, or \"\" for a name only a lookup can classify) and its key (host_key / Model.hostKey: what \"the same host\" compares) -- run by tests/test_destinations.py and tests/Model.test.js. `streams`: the helper's stream gate (stream_listen_refusal and is_stream_url; the model has none) -- the python suite. `streamHosts`: the helper's parse-time host rule for a channel URL against the playlist it came from (stream_host_refused; `source` is playlist_source's shape) -- the python suite. `hints`: the model's guide-hint verdict (Model.epgHintVerdict, with the active playlist's URL) -- the node suite; the helper's connect-time check is the binding layer behind it and is observed by tests/test_destinations.py against 127.0.0.1 servers. `refusals`: the reply the real helper gives for a redirect into a local address (tests/test_destinations.py composes it from a live run and compares), and the sentence the shell shows for it (Model.statusReason; Model.failureFromHost keeps the host) -- both suites. `env` and `destinationRules` are the names and the cache version the shell and the helper share.",
